# Oxford English: only the lines that differ from English (-ize spellings). The rest is English.

settings-help-topics-switcher-keywords = windows switch switcher alt tab open ring desktop show minimize clipboard copy paste history keyboard on screen

settings-help-topics-switcher-p1 = Open the ring and you'll see your open windows in a ring round the favourites. Each window has its own part, with its program's icon and name. Point at one and the middle shows a picture of that window. Click it to bring that window to the front, or right-click it for minimize, maximize and close. Pressing Alt and Tab also brings each open window to the front in turn.

settings-help-topics-keys-keywords = keys keyboard shortcuts super windows key alt tab screenshot print volume brightness lock terminal close maximize screen reader desktop show

settings-help-topics-keys-step2-8 = Super and Down: minimize the window. You can bring it back from the open windows in the ring.
